{title: 049 - Savior, Breathe an Evening Blessing}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #049 • EVENING PRAYER • 9.7.8.7}
{lyricist: James Edmeston}
{composer: George C. Stebbins}
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 49}
{meta: tune EVENING PRAYER}
{meta: meter 9.7.8.7}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Savior, [Db/Ab]breathe [G7]an [Cm/G]evening [Bb7]blessing,
[Ab]Ere [Db/Ab]repose [F7/A]our [Eb/Bb]spirits [Gdim]seal;
[Eb]Sin [Db/Ab]and [G7]want [Cm/G]we [Ab]come confessing;
[Ab]Thou canst [Db]save, and [Cm/G]Thou [Ab]canst heal.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Though [Db/Ab]the [G7]night [Cm/G]be [Ab]dark and [Bb7]dreary,
[Ab]Darkness cannot [Eb/Bb]hide [Db/Ab]from [Gdim]Thee;
[Eb]Thou [Db/Ab]art [G7]He [Cm/G]who, [Ab]never weary,
[Ab]Watchest [Db]where Thy [Cm/G]people [Ab]be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Though [Db/Ab]destruction [Ab]walk around [Eb/Bb]us.
[Ab]Though [Db/Ab]the [Ab]arrow [Eb/Bb]past [Db/Ab]us [Gdim]fly,
[Eb]Angel [G7]guards [Cm/G]from [Ab]Thee Surround [Gdim]us,
[Ab]We are [Db]safe if [Cm/G]Thou [Ab]art nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]Should swift [Db/Ab]death [G7]this [Cm/G]night [Ab]o're-take [Eb/Bb]us,
[Ab]And [Db/Ab]our [Ab]couch [F7/A]become [Db/Ab]our [Gdim]tomb,
[Eb]May [Db/Ab]the [G7]morn [Cm/G]of [Ab]glory wake [Gdim]us,
[Ab]Clad in [Db]light and [Cm/G]deathless [Ab]bloom.
{end_of_verse}
